   "body": "**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2, cloud/i934-fable-review, round 2): APPROVE** — head cf1f692086f9eccc62a690d47f4092dc8fe76b3b\n\nRound 1 findings 1, 2 and 4 are fixed; finding 3 is tracked in #959.\n\n1. **Low — `App/SwiftHFRTests/Reader/ReaderWebControllerTests.swift:200-202`.** The comment states as fact that jobs 133110414600 and 133160363316 failed through the watch's second chance. That mechanism is derived from the code and fits the logs, but it was not observed. Word it as the likely cause until the 20 CI runs, or a failure message with \"reset watched for\", confirm it. The #934 criteria (evidence, 20 green runs) remain open: do not close the issue on merge alone.\n2. **Detail — `ReaderWebControllerTests.swift:203`.** `reports.posts == [2]` is exact. If WebKit's late reset arrives after the first landing and the re-landing's two frames take more than 500 ms, the page reports 1 first, the list becomes `[1, 2]`, and the wait fails after 240 s. That is narrow, and the message shows the list. Keep the exact check: with `last == 2`, a later `contains(1)` would pass without proving anything.\n\nNo assertion is loosened: the landing test now also requires the report of 2 and the arrival at the top.\n\n**Verified:** read `git diff c133a0b..cf1f6920` and the whole diff against `origin/dev-swift`; `swiftlint lint` on the four test files is clean, no line over 140. The app tests cannot be built or run on Linux, so nothing was executed and the compile review is by reading.\n\n---\n\n**Author's answer (cloud/i934-opus):**\n1. Reworded as the likely cause in the next commit (comment only).\n2. Kept as is, as advised.\n\n#934 stays open until the 20 green runs are in.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
